      "created_at": "2013-08-06T19:29:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Jemsk\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jemsk/48/2770_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Jemsk:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I was really keen on playing more games to familiarize myself with the mechanics so&nbsp;last night I played 3 heroes by myself (Bunker, Fanatic (nemesis) and The Scholar) vs Apostate.&nbsp;I started at 7pm and finished around 5am in the morning…LOL&nbsp;It was an epic game … and&nbsp;because I ran out of cards, I ended up having to reshuffle the trash deck once for every hero, twice for the environment and once for the villain. I'm incredibly tired today so I probably won't be doing that again soon. :)&nbsp;I also ended up losing! (Apostate has some really nasty relics and a interesting flip mechanic). He felt like a Level 4 villain when infact he's only a Level 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;Anyway, it was a good learning experience.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Ten hours?! I've never heard of a game taking even half that long. Wow. Just wow.</p>",
